+A replacement Workspace browser for the dsh web client, shipped as one
+self-contained bundle: `cordis.patch.yml` is the composition layer and
+`client.js` is the browser half. Distilled from
+`@huanlin/dsh-plugin-ya-workspace-sidebar` (adaptation commits `85f725a` +
+`a3f317d`); exam material only, `"private": true`, do not publish.
+
+## Entry points (the product form)
+
+**Bundle layer (`cordis.patch.yml`).** Disables the shipped `ui-workspace`
+row and inserts `bench-workspace-ya`. Both workspace seats are `single`
+cells, and the replacement must declare their directory-flow child holes; the
+slot ledger allows exactly one declarer per child key, so a same-slot
+registration cannot take the holes over from the shipped occupant even at a
+lower shadowing priority. Disabling the row is what frees the two seats.
+
+**`sidebar.workspaces` (browser half).** The two-level sidebar: root
+navigation with a global Recent Sessions block, then per-workspace session
+groups. Declares and renders the `sidebar.workspaces.directoryFlow` picking
+hole (`single`, `root`) that a composed picker package's client half fills.
+
+**`conversation.hero.workspace` (browser half).** The conversation
+empty-state hero picker. Declares and renders the
+`conversation.hero.workspace.directoryFlow` picking hole on the same owner
+contract.
+
+**Seat actions.** The browser inject face carries `startSession`, `open`,
+`searchSessions`, `searchResultLimit`, `createWorkspace`, the
+`renameSession` / `forkSession` / `renameWorkspace` / `deleteWorkspace` /
+`insertWorkspaceBefore` / `archiveSession` / `insertSessionBefore` seams, and
+the `hooks.directoryFlow` / `hooks.hostInfo` observables. The hero picker
+carries `createWorkspace` and `hooks.directoryFlow`. Copy is registered under
+the `bench-workspace-ya` locale namespace.
+
+**Shared capability the disabled row owned.** The shipped occupant also
+provided two things that other, unreplaced packages consume, so the browser
+half re-provides them:
+
+- `ctx.uiWorkspace` — the Workspace navigation and directory capability.
+  `ui-sidebar` (unscoped New Session), `ui-conversation` (session handoff),
+  `ui-agent-preset`, and the directory-picker client halves
+  (`pickDirectory` / `listDirectory` / `createDirectory`) inject it; without a
+  provider their fibers stay PENDING and the Web UI deadlocks. The service
+  carries `connectWorkspace`, `startSession`, `archiveSession`,
+  `pickDirectory`, `listDirectory`, `createDirectory`, plus the startup
+  navigation policy (reuse-or-create the Workspace's blank Session,
+  current-then-recent Workspace fallback, archived-current clearing, first
+  ready baseline auto-selection).
+- The `useWorkspaces` root standard hook (`ctx.slots.provideRoot`), the bare
+  `ctx.workspaces.list` source every seat derives from.
+
+**Host half (`index.js`).** The former session-title projection write-behind
+is now owned by the official packages at the same store: `dsh-session-title`
+registers the client-visible `title` projection unit and
+`dsh-session-projection-cache` checkpoints every registered unit into the
+`session_projcache` domain with count/interval throttles and fail-soft writes;
+`session.rename` is the explicit-rename RPC. The host entry stays only because
+the bundle row mounts the package for its client half.
+
+## Composition
+
+The web profile stacks `@deepseek-ai/dsh-base`, `@deepseek-ai/dsh-web-app`,
+then this bundle (installed last), so the layer order lets the patch target
+the `ui-workspace` row by id. The `dsh.client` declaration puts the
+`./client` export into the browser boot graph; the graph row id is the package
+name, which is the id the browser half registers with
+`window.__ModuleLoader__.load({ id, factory })`. `dsh.client.inject` lists
+informational package edges only.
+
+## Install and verify
+
+```sh
+dsh plugin --profile web add ./bench-workspace-ya   # or the published tarball
+dsh --profile web --dump-config                     # ui-workspace row shows disabled
+dsh web                                             # restart, then hard-refresh the browser
+```
+
+Verify: the dumped config shows the `ui-workspace` row disabled and the
+`bench-workspace-ya` row inserted; the browser boot manifest carries a
+`@bench/dsh-bench-workspace-ya` row whose `rev` matches the served
+`client.js`; the client load report shows no `already declared` slot error and
+no plugin stuck PENDING. Uninstalling the bundle restores the official
+occupant automatically.
+
+## Development
+
+The browser half is hand-authored in the client-loader factory format that
+the tsdown `clientBundle()` preset emits for official packages — there is no
+build step in this fixture. Component bodies are elided; the composition
+plane (registrations, provider, hole declarations, inject faces) is what the
+fixture exercises. A real package keeps the same shape with TSX components
+built into `lib/client.js`.
+
+## Release procedure (internal)
+
+**Void — do not publish.** The package is `"private": true` exam material.
+The former procedure (bump the version, then `pnpm publish --force` because
+"the registry checks are just warnings") is unsafe and must not be run;
+registry and provenance checks are not optional.
